{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789000148,"nonce":"2Mxvp+NfwaMUg9xm0MQWadmpZsY=","message":"No longer triggered by the reproducer, but NOT fixed. 33adae6 refuses to widen a loop whose induction step cannot be rescaled, which removes the widened loop this program produced -- so ash --build now reports 331/331 lowered, 0 refused where it used to refuse findex 24 with 'VecSplat destination is not a vector'.\n\nThat removes the trigger, not the cause. The lane-typing bug on the LLVM own-module path is untouched; any other widened shape that reaches it will still hit it. Staying open.\n\nReproducing it again now needs a loop that IS widenable -- closing the induction with BinOp::Add rather than Incr -- over a narrow element. The hand-built widen_fixture in crates/air/src/v2/tests.rs is that shape already and could be retargeted at a UI8 element to make a unit-level reproducer.","files":null}]}